🧱 1. Jenkins Basics (Foundations)

You gotta start by really understanding how Jenkins thinks. Learn:

Installation & Configuration (both on local and server)

Jenkins UI navigation — jobs, builds, workspace, console output

Freestyle jobs — how to run shell commands, trigger builds manually, etc.

Build triggers — cron (poll SCM), GitHub webhook, manual, and upstream jobs

Build artifacts — storing, archiving, and sharing between stages

Once you’re comfy with that, move on to pipelines 👇

⚙️ 2. Jenkins Pipelines (Core DevOps Skill)

Pipelines are the real magic. You’ll need to be fluent in:

Declarative vs. Scripted pipelines

Pipeline syntax (pipeline { agent any ... })

Stages, steps, and environment variables

Post actions (success, failure, always)

Parameters (string, boolean, choice, credentials)

Using Jenkinsfile in Git (code as configuration)

Parallel stages — running tests or builds in parallel

👉 You should be able to write a Jenkinsfile from scratch that builds, tests, and deploys a simple app.

🔗 3. Integrations (DevOps Glue)

DevOps is all about tools talking to each other. Learn how Jenkins integrates with:

Git/GitHub/GitLab/Bitbucket for SCM

Docker for building and deploying containers

Ansible for configuration management and deployments

Kubernetes for CI/CD on clusters

Slack/MS Teams for build notifications

JIRA or ServiceNow for tracking

💡 Practice tip: Set up a small Jenkins pipeline that clones code from GitHub, builds a Docker image, pushes it to Docker Hub, and deploys it via Ansible.

🧰 4. Plugins & Extensibility

Jenkins is all about plugins. The must-know ones:

Git Plugin

Pipeline Plugin

Blue Ocean

Credentials Binding

Email Extension

Slack Notifier

Docker Plugin

AnsiColor, Timestamper, etc.

Know how to install, configure, and manage plugin versions (especially in production).

🔒 5. Jenkins Security & Administration

A true DevOps engineer owns their Jenkins environment. Learn:

User authentication & authorization (RBAC)

Credentials management (SSH keys, tokens)

Securing Jenkins with HTTPS

Backup & restore strategies

Scaling Jenkins (master-agent setup)

🐳 6. Jenkins + Docker + Kubernetes

This combo is where modern CI/CD lives. Practice:

Running Jenkins inside Docker

Using Docker agents in pipelines

Deploying to Kubernetes using Jenkins (Jenkins X, or K8s plugin)

Managing Jenkins as code with JCasC (Jenkins Configuration as Code)

📈 7. Real-World CI/CD Scenarios

Now put it all together:

Build → Test → Package → Deploy → Notify

Handle rollback and versioning

Use blue/green or canary deployments

Set up multi-environment pipelines (dev, staging, prod)

🧠 8. Bonus: Automation + Observability

Automate Jenkins updates and plugin management

Set up monitoring with Prometheus + Grafana

Integrate Jenkins logs with ELK / Loki
